1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,420
[JESTER 10-A (M)]
The big day is coming!

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,170
Lord Aldarp's marriage!

3
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:05,590
[laughing]

4
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:08,180
[KAZUMA] Guess ole Aldarp
must be in a pretty big hurry.

5
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:09,760
'Cause it looks like
he's putting everything else

6
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,390
on hold to announce
the wedding date.

7
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:13,140
[indistinct chatter]

8
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:16,480
[MEGUMIN] This isn't the time
to be pouting, Kazuma!

9
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,140
[blowing]

10
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:21,810
[KAZUMA] Listen, I told you,
it was her decision.

11
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,150
And I'm not doing squat 'til
she comes crying for my help.

12
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:25,570
[growls]

13
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:28,530
- Hey!
- Sorry, I don't accept that!

14
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:30,740
If you're just going to wait
for that day and do nothing,

15
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:32,620
then I'll take action myself!

16
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,830
Go ahead, as long as it's not
too violent, all right?

17
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,540
And gimme that thing back.

18
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:39,830
You have no idea how long
I've been working on it.

19
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,380
[MEGUMIN]
Ahh.

20
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:43,840
What is this exactly?

21
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,460
[sighs]

22
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:46,880
See the bubbles?

23
00:00:46,970 --> 00:00:48,300
You can pop 'em.

24
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:51,680
It relieves stress and it's
a lotta fun to play with, too.

25
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,390
Is that all it does?

26
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:56,810
[KAZUMA]
Uh-huh.

27
00:00:58,940 --> 00:00:59,940
[grunts]

28
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:01,020
♪

29
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:02,190
[screams]

30
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:35,200
- [sighs]
- Oh, hey, uh...

31
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,700
I'm afraid this is quite
an urgent matter.

32
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:40,330
I've come here with a request,
Master Satou.

33
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,500
♪

34
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:44,500
[KAZUMA] Has Darkness finally
swallowed her pride

35
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:47,130
and admitted
that she needs my help?

36
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:49,170
What?

37
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:51,710
[MEGUMIN] "This warning
is for the Dustiness family.

38
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,720
A confidential source
has indicated that

39
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:56,260
one of the Devil King's
generals will be carrying out

40
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:59,810
an imminent attack on Axel's
chapel of the Eris Sect.

41
00:02:59,890 --> 00:03:02,220
It has been scheduled
for the day of the wedding!

42
00:03:02,310 --> 00:03:05,190
If the upcoming ceremony
is not canceled immediately,

43
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:07,600
the entire chapel
will be caught in a fiery blast

44
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:09,480
of Explosion magic!"

45
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:13,320
"For everybody's sake I hope
this letter is taken seriously

46
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,240
from a concerned wizard."

47
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,860
[KAZUMA]
I'm so sorry about this!

48
00:03:16,950 --> 00:03:19,620
I'm gonna tear that
maniac a new one!

49
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:23,660
Megumin you better
get your butt out here!

50
00:03:23,750 --> 00:03:27,420
And so, the days passed by
without Darkness.

51
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,840
I'd made up my mind about
letting the whole thing go

52
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:31,960
but the others...

53
00:03:32,050 --> 00:03:35,380
[AQUA] Now, watch in amazement
as I pull a Rookie Slayer

54
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:36,970
out of this tiny little basket!

55
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:38,760
Don't pull crap like that
outta there!

56
00:03:38,850 --> 00:03:40,260
Hey, what do you think
you're doing?

57
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:41,760
You need to let go of me,
all right?

58
00:03:41,850 --> 00:03:43,520
Just take a look at all the
people who showed up

59
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,850
to see my awesome tricks!

60
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:47,190
[KAZUMA] Yeah, that's the
reason they called me here!

61
00:03:47,270 --> 00:03:49,150
To do something about
the ruckus outside the house!

62
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,860
Hey, hurry it up
and do the trick!

63
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,780
[MAN 10-C (M)]
Right on with the show!

64
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:56,280
Please, I can't accept
donations from you.

65
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,610
I'm not a real entertainer,
so you can all just hold on

66
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,620
to your money, okay?

67
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:03,200
[AQUA] Kazuma this is all
a part of my master plan

68
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:05,200
to try and lure Darkness
out of her house.

69
00:04:05,290 --> 00:04:06,870
- What?
- Yeah!

70
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,710
You know the legend
about the Amano-Iwato,

71
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:10,210
don't you, Kazuma?

72
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:11,710
- It's the same!
- [sighs]

73
00:04:11,790 --> 00:04:13,050
[AQUA]
Yo, Darkness!

74
00:04:13,130 --> 00:04:14,380
I know you're listening!

75
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:16,300
Hurry up and come out!

76
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:19,260
You're really gonna regret
not seeing this in person!

77
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,970
'Cause I'm gonna pull off
my best...

78
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:22,930
- [growls]
- Kazuma!

79
00:04:23,010 --> 00:04:24,390
What the heck do you
think you're doing?

80
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:25,680
You better let go of me!

81
00:04:25,770 --> 00:04:27,060
[KAZUMA]
We're heading home right now!

82
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:28,940
Wait you can't
drag me away, yet!

83
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:29,850
I've got more tricks!

84
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:32,150
I'm doing them every day
till she comes out!

85
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,980
[AQUA]
You hear me, Darkness?

86
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:37,070
Darkness!
Darkness!

87
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:38,700
[KAZUMA]
And a few days after that.

88
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,450
[groaning sigh]

89
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:45,240
Can't believe
I'm finally back here.

90
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:47,500
It's been three days, I think?

91
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:50,170
I already told ya,
you were gonna get arrested

92
00:04:50,250 --> 00:04:51,250
for sending in those threats.

93
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:52,580
[thuds]

94
00:04:52,670 --> 00:04:53,750
♪

95
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:56,090
[KAZUMA]
Just settle down, okay?

96
00:04:56,170 --> 00:04:57,380
- 'Cause as far as I can tell...
- [slurps]

97
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:58,630
...all you and Aqua have done

98
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,510
is annoy the Dustiness Family.

99
00:05:00,590 --> 00:05:01,930
♪

100
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:04,010
[MEGUMIN] In that case,
don't you think it's about time

101
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:05,470
you started helping out?

102
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,770
Uh!

103
00:05:06,850 --> 00:05:09,190
Not until I hear something
from Darkness.

104
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:10,480
[thudding]

105
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:11,810
You're really awful!

106
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:14,110
The townspeople may
call you names like Kazutrash

107
00:05:14,270 --> 00:05:16,480
and Crapuma
but, at the end of the day

108
00:05:16,570 --> 00:05:18,190
I always thought you
were the kind of person

109
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:19,780
that would come through
for your friends

110
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:21,910
and lend a hand
when they need it the most.

111
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:23,070
[growling softly]

112
00:05:25,030 --> 00:05:26,450
[sighs]

113
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:29,250
The man that I love
and care for.

114
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:33,330
He might complain
the whole time.

115
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:37,880
But when it really matters
I know he'd still come through.

116
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,340
That's what he's like.

117
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:42,220
♪

118
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,590
Lemme guess. You think
I'm just gonna roll over

119
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:46,760
if you throw in the word
"love," don't ya?

120
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:49,810
So sorry,
but I'm not that easy.

121
00:05:49,890 --> 00:05:51,730
[scoffs]

122
00:05:51,810 --> 00:05:55,060
[KAZUMA] Knock it off!
Ha, you know I'm ticklish.

123
00:05:55,150 --> 00:05:58,070
[indistinct chatter]

124
00:05:58,150 --> 00:06:01,320
[KAZUMA] Before long the day
of Darkness' wedding

125
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:03,110
finally arrived.

126
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,570
[blowing]

127
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:06,780
Let's get going, Kazuma!

128
00:06:06,870 --> 00:06:08,660
It's about time
for us to crash a wedding!

129
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:09,740
[chuckles]

130
00:06:09,830 --> 00:06:12,710
Uh-oh, a spell slipped
and the place was destroyed.

131
00:06:12,790 --> 00:06:14,670
Oops, a spell slipped
and the lord's estate

132
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:16,040
was totally decimated!

133
00:06:16,130 --> 00:06:18,090
Accidents happen!

134
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:20,630
[KAZUMA]
Don't do it, I'm serious.

135
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:22,420
It won't just end with debt.

136
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:25,180
You'd be a real criminal
this time around.

137
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,970
You'll regret
not going with me!

138
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:29,390
[KAZUMA]
Count me out.

139
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:31,350
[gasping]

140
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:33,140
[whimpering]

141
00:06:33,230 --> 00:06:34,390
Come on, Kazuma!

142
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:36,020
So what that lord
might do to Darkness

143
00:06:36,110 --> 00:06:37,560
doesn't even bother you?

144
00:06:37,650 --> 00:06:40,320
Are you kidding me?
You don't care about her?

145
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,440
Of course, I do, damn it!

146
00:06:42,530 --> 00:06:43,820
[gasps]

147
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:47,070
[KAZUMA]
How could I not care?

148
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:49,240
Uh-huh...
[sighs]

149
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:52,830
Maybe you haven't
heard about this

150
00:06:52,910 --> 00:06:55,290
but that old creep
he'll do anything

151
00:06:55,370 --> 00:06:57,750
to get his disgusting hands
on a woman.

152
00:06:57,830 --> 00:07:00,590
And then when he's bored,
he just turns around

153
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,210
and throws 'em out.

154
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:05,630
The worst part is
he does this over and over.

155
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:08,800
Though, somehow, there's never
any evidence to prove it.

156
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:10,720
I can't stand that bastard!

157
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:13,560
♪

158
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:15,310
Then, you have to help!

159
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:16,400
At least try!

160
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,900
Surely you can come up
with some kind

161
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:19,440
of underhanded scheme!

162
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,610
♪

163
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:23,530
[KAZUMA] There's nothing
I can do this time.

164
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:27,660
This is a wedding
between two nobles

165
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:29,490
and there's tight security.

166
00:07:29,570 --> 00:07:33,370
So, it would be impossible
for us to make any moves.

167
00:07:33,450 --> 00:07:35,370
Our hands are tied on this one.

168
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:37,420
That's the reason
I've been waiting for Darkness

169
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,710
to reach out.

170
00:07:39,790 --> 00:07:41,840
Kazuma.

171
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:45,050
Her Father's in bed
and really ill.

172
00:07:45,130 --> 00:07:46,470
And we don't have
any connections

173
00:07:46,550 --> 00:07:47,760
to other nobles here.

174
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:53,680
Fact is, I'm just a poor
adventuring loser.

175
00:07:53,770 --> 00:07:55,180
[sighs]

176
00:07:55,270 --> 00:07:56,690
♪

177
00:07:56,770 --> 00:07:59,150
[KAZUMA] Chalk it up to our
different stations, I guess.

178
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:01,480
[sighs]
After all...

179
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:05,240
Darkness comes from
a different world than we do.

180
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,150
Just being able to go
adventuring with her

181
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:10,700
for so long
was basically a miracle.

182
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:12,660
♪

183
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,160
[sighs]

184
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:16,620
[footsteps]

185
00:08:16,710 --> 00:08:19,380
♪

186
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:25,800
Kazuma you have been
thinking of ways to stop this.

187
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:28,880
I get it, now
and that's enough for me.

188
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:32,300
Huh?

189
00:08:32,390 --> 00:08:34,970
That said I have
to think this through

190
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:36,810
and try to do what's best.

191
00:08:36,890 --> 00:08:37,980
All right?

192
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,560
But, you should, too.

193
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,810
That way you can look back
and have no regrets.

194
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:44,940
♪

195
00:08:45,030 --> 00:08:46,440
I'll leave you to it.

196
00:08:46,530 --> 00:08:48,070
[door creaking opens]

197
00:08:49,450 --> 00:08:50,780
[door closes]

198
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:53,080
♪

199
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,410
[KAZUMA]
It is what it is.

200
00:08:55,490 --> 00:08:56,700
Hello there!

201
00:08:56,790 --> 00:08:58,750
Your fickle "friends"
may have left you

202
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:01,380
but the all-seeing demon
has come to help!

203
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,460
Vanir?

204
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:04,040
You may feel it wise
to dance madly

205
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:06,420
while crying tears
of joy at my arrival!

206
00:09:06,510 --> 00:09:08,130
Now then, why don't we
take a good look

207
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:10,430
at the fruits
of your knowledge?

208
00:09:10,510 --> 00:09:11,510
Huh?

209
00:09:11,590 --> 00:09:13,680
Do you seriously believe
I'm in any shape

210
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:15,390
to negotiate business with you?

211
00:09:15,470 --> 00:09:18,180
I want to talk to that
pretty owner, right now!

212
00:09:18,270 --> 00:09:20,190
That little debt-maker
couldn't negotiate

213
00:09:20,270 --> 00:09:22,190
her way out of a paper bag.

214
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:24,400
Yesterday, she walks up
to me and says,

215
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,650
"This is going to be a massive
hit with adventurer couples!"

216
00:09:27,730 --> 00:09:30,240
[VANIR] Then, she goes
and stocks this pendant!

217
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,700
What is that thing?

218
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:34,660
If the one who wears it
is ever fatally injured

219
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,080
then the last embers
of their life

220
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:38,950
ignite a rather
spectacular explosion!

221
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:40,710
[VANIR]
The concept is...

222
00:09:40,790 --> 00:09:43,920
In your last remaining moments
you can draw your final breath

223
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,040
knowing you've protected
your beloved!

224
00:09:46,130 --> 00:09:49,050
Isn't that the most
romantic thing ever?

225
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,760
Needless to say, she was
thrilled with the notion!

226
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:54,800
Yet the eruption is so volatile
that it blows away

227
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:57,760
not only the enemy,
but the beloved as well!

228
00:09:57,850 --> 00:10:00,020
What better example
of the owner's "questionable"

229
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:03,100
entrepreneurial sense
could you ask for?

230
00:10:03,190 --> 00:10:05,150
Care to make a purchase?

231
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:07,190
Nah, I'm good.

232
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:10,320
Hey, wait a minute you said
you're here to help me?

233
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:12,150
[VANIR]
Ohh!

234
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:14,370
I can see you've been
continuing product development,

235
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:16,830
as I so wisely advised.

236
00:10:16,910 --> 00:10:18,660
Which brings me to...

237
00:10:18,740 --> 00:10:20,580
♪

238
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:22,540
[gasps]

239
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:24,830
N-Now listen, Vanir,
these are the only ideas

240
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,130
that I've got left, okay?

241
00:10:26,210 --> 00:10:28,920
And I won't let them go
for less than they're worth.

242
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,840
Such a paradoxical man.

243
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:33,340
You, the one who's desperate
to rescue the armored girl,

244
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:35,720
but feels terrified
by rejection!

245
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:38,600
The all-seeing Vanir
officially declares.

246
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:40,350
In exchange
for the intellectual rights

247
00:10:40,430 --> 00:10:42,810
to your ideas
you will gladly accept

248
00:10:42,890 --> 00:10:46,360
this incredibly
generous bag of money!

249
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:48,480
[laughs]

250
00:10:48,570 --> 00:10:51,280
Now if you'll simply allow me
to verify the products

251
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,490
and rights involved.

252
00:10:52,570 --> 00:10:56,490
Hey, listen, you know
all kinds of stuff, right?

253
00:10:56,570 --> 00:10:57,580
Well, of course.

254
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,490
I can see just about anything.

255
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:02,250
For instance, I already have
the answer to the questions

256
00:11:02,330 --> 00:11:03,540
you're about to ask me.

257
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,710
Huh.

258
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:06,880
[VANIR] Why in the world
is armor girl in debt

259
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:09,500
to this odious lord,
in the first place?

260
00:11:09,590 --> 00:11:12,880
How is it, that despite his
rather vulgar appetites,

261
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:16,760
there's no evidence of that
man's debauchery whatsoever?

262
00:11:16,930 --> 00:11:18,930
Hey, you're a demon, so--

263
00:11:19,010 --> 00:11:21,010
[VANIR] "So why are you
trying to be so helpful

264
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,140
all of a sudden?"

265
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:24,230
"Are you plotting something?"

266
00:11:24,310 --> 00:11:26,600
And, the answer to that is,
"most certainly."

267
00:11:26,690 --> 00:11:28,190
I am a demon, after all.

268
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:31,020
But in this particular case
our interests are aligned.

269
00:11:31,110 --> 00:11:33,530
So, I'm offering you
a helping hand.

270
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:34,610
How so?

271
00:11:34,690 --> 00:11:36,910
Let's begin with the secret
ideas you've been saving

272
00:11:36,990 --> 00:11:38,490
in case of an emergency.

273
00:11:38,570 --> 00:11:41,740
I may well purchase them
at a discount on this day.

274
00:11:41,830 --> 00:11:42,990
[KAZUMA]
Oh, man!

275
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:45,830
All-seeing demons
are the worst.

276
00:11:45,910 --> 00:11:48,040
Anyway, if you really
have my answers,

277
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,590
could you stop holding out
and tell me, already?

278
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:51,880
Most assuredly.

279
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:53,840
Let me enlighten you!

280
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:56,470
Sacred Exorcism!

281
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,800
[laughter]

282
00:12:00,350 --> 00:12:02,640
Whoa, you're
an archdemon, aren't ya?

283
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:04,680
How could you let
a plumbing Goddess do you in?

284
00:12:04,770 --> 00:12:06,980
Huh, I leave you alone here
for five minutes

285
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,940
and now you're some
kinda demon worshiper?

286
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,770
And I'm a Water Goddess,
I'll have you know!

287
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,820
Do ya think you could
ever not butt in?

288
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:14,360
You were the one who left!

289
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:16,990
Hey, I was making sure
our guest was all right!

290
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,820
What are you even
talking about?

291
00:12:18,910 --> 00:12:21,660
[KAZUMA] How could you...
The butler?

292
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:24,990
If you're preoccupied,
then I can just excuse myself.

293
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:27,750
Pardon me, sir, good day.

294
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:30,880
Oh, no, this is just...

295
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,840
[chuckles]

296
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:35,250
[VANIR] Devious attack
you thug of a Goddess!

297
00:12:35,340 --> 00:12:36,340
Just look!

298
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:39,220
Do you see the crack
you've put on my amazing mask!

299
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:40,800
Oh, I'm sorry.

300
00:12:40,890 --> 00:12:42,350
Think you could
ever forgive me?

301
00:12:42,430 --> 00:12:44,520
I didn't realize I needed
to ask someone's permission

302
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:45,890
to exterminate a pest.

303
00:12:45,970 --> 00:12:47,270
What are ya, stupid?

304
00:12:47,350 --> 00:12:48,980
[snickering]

305
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:52,270
[KAZUMA]
Konosu Butt out?

306
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:55,230
[VANIR] Now then lad who finds
himself forsaken by the Gods,

307
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:58,280
despite his extreme proximity
to one of them.

308
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,780
Per our conversation
you were a bit curious

309
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:02,740
about the armor girl's
debt, yes?

310
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,700
[KAZUMA]
R-Right.

311
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:06,160
Interestingly...

312
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:09,160
the entire thing began
when you adventurers

313
00:13:09,250 --> 00:13:11,380
brought down the
Mobile Fortress Destroyer.

314
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:12,580
The Destroyer?

315
00:13:12,670 --> 00:13:13,840
♪

316
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:14,710
Go on.

317
00:13:14,790 --> 00:13:17,340
When such a grand weapon
makes its presence felt

318
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:20,300
a lord's land is devastated.

319
00:13:20,380 --> 00:13:22,470
[VANIR] That wasn't the case
in this town, however,

320
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:25,300
thanks to your
ludicrous struggles.

321
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:27,020
But isn't that a good thing?

322
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:28,770
[VANIR]
The town itself was spared

323
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:31,560
but there were myriad
of other concerns.

324
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:34,310
Such as the farmlands
surrounding it,

325
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,730
which were trampled
under the weight

326
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:38,150
of that eight-legged machine.

327
00:13:38,230 --> 00:13:40,530
The ones who were tasked
with tending to those areas

328
00:13:40,610 --> 00:13:42,490
effectively lost everything.

329
00:13:42,570 --> 00:13:44,160
- Uh.
- And all of those peasants

330
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,530
turned to the lord of the land

331
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:47,160
in their time of need.

332
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:48,540
[groaning]

333
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:51,290
Quite right, it was exactly
as you'd imagine!

334
00:13:51,370 --> 00:13:53,710
And what was
his chosen response?

335
00:13:53,790 --> 00:13:56,000
[ALDARP] Consider the fact
that you survived at all

336
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:57,130
to be a victory.

337
00:13:57,210 --> 00:13:58,460
But do be patient.

338
00:13:58,550 --> 00:14:00,920
"Things will start
growing again, in time."

339
00:14:01,010 --> 00:14:02,180
He said.

340
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:03,840
[both whimpering]

341
00:14:03,930 --> 00:14:05,970
Ascribing the damage
to a natural disaster

342
00:14:06,050 --> 00:14:08,430
didn't ease
their many troubles.

343
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:10,140
These people were desperate.

344
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:13,440
So, they came crying
to the Dustiness family,

345
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,350
with whom you're acquainted.

346
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:18,440
And this was their
impassioned plea.

347
00:14:18,530 --> 00:14:20,440
[VANIR] Lord Dustiness,
who reimbursed damages

348
00:14:20,530 --> 00:14:22,650
caused by the
adventurers' flooding!"

349
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:24,700
Tell us you'll find it
in your generous heart

350
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:26,070
to give us aid yet again.

351
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:27,740
We're begging you!"

352
00:14:27,830 --> 00:14:29,200
-"Oh, please."
- [gasps]

353
00:14:29,290 --> 00:14:30,580
Wait, what did you say?

354
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:33,420
Something about the
buildings damaged in the flood?

355
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:35,210
Mm-ha.

356
00:14:35,290 --> 00:14:37,500
Remember back when you were
asked to pay for the damages

357
00:14:37,590 --> 00:14:39,340
that your little group caused?

358
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:42,130
[VANIR] You weren't expected
to cover the costs, completely.

359
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:45,430
In fact, it was only
a portion, wasn't it?

360
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:47,810
Seems the Dustiness family
lost a majority

361
00:14:47,890 --> 00:14:49,140
of their considerable wealth

362
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:51,430
paying for the destruction
the flood created.

363
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:52,390
[gasps]

364
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:55,440
And yet, despite that to aid
those whose livelihoods

365
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,270
were crushed by the Destroyer.

366
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:58,690
[VANIR]
They bowed to the local lord,

367
00:14:58,770 --> 00:15:02,150
who shunned his own duties,
and borrowed the needed sum.

368
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,280
With one particular
stipulation.

369
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:05,910
♪

370
00:15:05,990 --> 00:15:07,990
Now, if you have trouble
paying back the loan

371
00:15:08,070 --> 00:15:09,660
for any reason whatsoever,

372
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:12,410
you can always use
your body as collateral.

373
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:14,000
[grunts]

374
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:16,500
[growling]

375
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:18,000
Oh, Kazuma.

376
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:21,340
Your hand must be in pain after
slamming the table like that.

377
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,710
I'm sure it's hurting you.

378
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:26,800
[KAZUMA]
That would explain everything.

379
00:15:26,890 --> 00:15:29,850
How much money does
Darkness actually owe him?

380
00:15:29,930 --> 00:15:31,850
[chuckles]

381
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:34,270
[VANIR] If we take the total
value of your personal assets

382
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:36,390
and add up the contents
of this bag,

383
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:38,610
it should just
about cover the cost.

384
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:44,280
Now then shall we discuss
our business?

385
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,530
[indistinct chatter]

386
00:15:46,610 --> 00:15:48,700
♪

387
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:50,620
You look beautiful, Milady.

388
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:52,240
So lovely.

389
00:15:52,330 --> 00:15:54,080
Once the wedding ceremony
is over,

390
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:56,670
I think you should visit
the master at the mansion.

391
00:15:56,750 --> 00:15:58,540
Then, he'll be able
to see you in this dress

392
00:15:58,630 --> 00:16:00,250
Hmm.

393
00:16:00,330 --> 00:16:01,800
- [ALDARP] Move aside!
- [gasps]

394
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:04,050
In a matter of moments,
Lalatina will be mine.

395
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:05,130
Understand?

396
00:16:05,210 --> 00:16:07,760
I do understand, sir,
but I'm afraid only members

397
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,800
of the Dustiness family
may enter.

398
00:16:09,890 --> 00:16:10,930
I must ask you to leave.

399
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:12,100
You idiot!

400
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:14,470
Obviously, you don't seem
to realize that

401
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:17,190
after the nuptials,
I will be your employer!

402
00:16:17,270 --> 00:16:19,690
That may be true
but, you can't pass

403
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,520
as I am not yet your employee.

404
00:16:21,610 --> 00:16:24,110
[growls]

405
00:16:24,190 --> 00:16:26,610
Well, I'll remember
your smug face!

406
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:28,860
Just you wait until
the wedding is over!

407
00:16:28,950 --> 00:16:30,620
[sighs]

408
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:32,740
[DARKNESS] Could you please
call the guard for me?

409
00:16:32,830 --> 00:16:34,200
I would like to thank him.

410
00:16:34,290 --> 00:16:36,160
O-Of course.

411
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:37,500
[door creaking opens]

412
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:38,960
Come in.

413
00:16:43,130 --> 00:16:45,000
Oh, Lady Dustiness.

414
00:16:45,090 --> 00:16:46,590
You look so beautiful.

415
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:50,590
You refused him
and I thank you.

416
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:53,510
I will make certain
you are not punished for that.

417
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:55,470
You needn't worry.

418
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:57,850
I would've been quite
honored to serve any man

419
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,650
you had chosen, however.

420
00:17:01,150 --> 00:17:03,190
A man that I had chosen, huh?

421
00:17:03,270 --> 00:17:04,940
[chuckles]

422
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:06,070
[chuckles]

423
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:09,110
If I may say, I feel
happy enough seeing you smiling

424
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:12,030
in light of the
current situation.

425
00:17:12,110 --> 00:17:13,950
[footsteps]

426
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:19,920
And this may be rather
impertinent of me

427
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,540
but considering how
truly ravishing you are

428
00:17:22,630 --> 00:17:24,750
engaging in such
frenzied personal play

429
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:26,380
may be a bad idea.

430
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:28,130
[door closes]

431
00:17:28,210 --> 00:17:29,630
[whimpering]

432
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:30,880
This is his fault!

433
00:17:30,970 --> 00:17:34,010
Kazuma and all those
ridiculous impersonations!

434
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:36,260
[sighs]

435
00:17:36,350 --> 00:17:37,770
♪

436
00:17:37,850 --> 00:17:39,940
[DARKNESS] While there may be
a few exceptions

437
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:41,440
most people
who are born to nobility

438
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:45,360
are never really able to live
life as they would like.

439
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:48,740
But, in spite of that
I was so fortunate

440
00:17:48,820 --> 00:17:50,990
as I spent the majority
of my time around those

441
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,070
with whom I could be myself.

442
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,990
And that is enough.

443
00:17:55,070 --> 00:17:57,870
Asking for any more
would only be selfish.

444
00:17:57,950 --> 00:18:00,830
Now it is my turn to repay
the people of this town.

445
00:18:00,910 --> 00:18:02,500
♪

446
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:04,040
[MAID 10-A (F)]
Milady?

447
00:18:04,130 --> 00:18:05,670
Oh, sorry.

448
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:07,500
Forgive me.

449
00:18:07,590 --> 00:18:09,460
[DARKNESS] I wonder how the
others in our group would react

450
00:18:09,550 --> 00:18:11,220
if they ever found out
about my debt.

451
00:18:13,090 --> 00:18:15,180
Megumin would be furious.

452
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:19,100
Aqua would start crying out
of nowhere, more than likely.

453
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:22,940
And as for him, he would
probably call me an idiot,

454
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:24,770
then give an unbelievably
long lecture

455
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:27,520
while harassing me
with pinpoint accuracy

456
00:18:27,610 --> 00:18:29,480
before trying something
to save me.

457
00:18:29,570 --> 00:18:31,240
♪

458
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:35,360
Will he come here today?

459
00:18:35,450 --> 00:18:36,450
♪

460
00:18:36,530 --> 00:18:38,660
No, certainly not.

461
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:42,080
Knowing him, he is holed up
in the mansion, sulking,

462
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:44,750
with a sour look on his face.

463
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:46,290
Hmm.

464
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:47,840
[knocking]

465
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,920
[HAGEN]
It's time to begin, Milady.

466
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:51,800
The priest presiding
over the ceremony

467
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,840
is one who's very
well respected

468
00:18:53,930 --> 00:18:57,010
and from what I understand,
the finest in town.

469
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:59,810
I'm quite certain this will be
a wonderful occasion.

470
00:18:59,890 --> 00:19:01,640
♪

471
00:19:01,730 --> 00:19:04,520
[DARKNESS] I had such
an unforgettable time.

472
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:07,860
Truly, this year with the
others has been very special.

473
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:08,940
[light background chatter]

474
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:12,070
[DARKNESS] Every day was
so much fun and so joyful.

475
00:19:12,150 --> 00:19:13,570
[light background chatter]

476
00:19:16,950 --> 00:19:18,240
[sighs]

477
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:20,280
[indistinct chatter]

478
00:19:20,370 --> 00:19:21,830
[SAKAMAKI]
Quit shoving, damn it!

479
00:19:21,910 --> 00:19:23,710
I still can't see inside!

480
00:19:23,790 --> 00:19:26,000
[indistinct chatter]

481
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,830
I just want you to know,
I'll be praying

482
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,710
for your happiness, Milady.

483
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:30,960
Hmm.

484
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,550
♪

485
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:55,860
♪

486
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:08,580
Hmm. Ooh!

487
00:20:08,670 --> 00:20:10,920
♪

488
00:20:16,260 --> 00:20:18,090
[evil chuckle]

489
00:20:18,180 --> 00:20:19,970
♪

490
00:20:32,020 --> 00:20:33,480
Ahh, well...

491
00:20:33,570 --> 00:20:37,280
you Darkness, are here today,
to take this old man,

492
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:39,530
who looks just like a cross
between a pig and a bear.

493
00:20:39,610 --> 00:20:40,610
- [gasps]
- A pig?

494
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:42,240
[AQUA (PRIEST)] In keeping
with the laws laid down

495
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:43,790
by some other God, not me

496
00:20:43,870 --> 00:20:47,040
and being pressured into a
marriage against your own will.

497
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:51,920
In sickness and in health,
in good times and bad,

498
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,960
for richer and for poorer.

499
00:20:54,050 --> 00:20:56,010
Will you love this old man?

500
00:20:56,090 --> 00:20:57,840
Honor this old man?

501
00:20:57,920 --> 00:20:59,720
Treasure this old man?

502
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,340
- Aid this old man?
- [indistinct chatter]

503
00:21:01,430 --> 00:21:03,010
Cherish this old man?

504
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:04,810
Tend to this old man?

505
00:21:04,890 --> 00:21:09,100
And adore this old man
for the rest of your days,

506
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:10,810
- until death do you part?
- [whimpering]

507
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:12,730
I'm not an old man!

508
00:21:12,810 --> 00:21:14,440
Of course, you can't do that.

509
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,860
So, I say we should leave here
and head home,

510
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:20,530
then chow down on the food
Kazuma made for us!

511
00:21:20,610 --> 00:21:22,950
After that, we'll all sit
around and drink bubbly!

512
00:21:23,030 --> 00:21:24,200
[all gasping]

513
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:25,530
Wait, I know you!

514
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:28,210
You're the same woman who came
to my luxurious mansion

515
00:21:28,290 --> 00:21:29,920
and made a complete mess of it!

516
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,250
[gasps]

517
00:21:31,330 --> 00:21:33,210
♪

518
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:40,050
[KAZUMA]
Hi, Dad. Hi, Mom.

519
00:21:40,130 --> 00:21:43,140
I just wanted to let you know
your adorable son

520
00:21:43,220 --> 00:21:45,760
who you raised to be
a pretty normal boy

521
00:21:45,850 --> 00:21:47,270
is about to say "goodbye"
to all of that now.

522
00:21:47,350 --> 00:21:49,350
[AQUA]
Go, Kazuma get her!

523
00:21:49,430 --> 00:21:50,980
[KAZUMA] Considering
I'm picking' a fight

524
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:53,190
with the biggest
bigshot around here,

525
00:21:53,690 --> 00:21:56,070
not to mention kidnapping
a noble lady!

526
00:21:56,150 --> 00:21:57,570
[gasps]

527
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:59,110
Let's go home, Darkness!

528
00:23:31,040 --> 00:23:32,540
[GROUP]
Dear Devil King!

529
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:33,620
- [HANS] We!
- [VERDIA] We!

530
00:23:33,700 --> 00:23:34,750
[SYLVIA]
All of us!

531
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:38,250
[GROUP] Will enjoy living
on the banks of the river Styx!

532
00:23:38,420 --> 00:23:39,920
[SYLVIA]
And endeavor to continue...

